nerates candidate hypotheses through grounded LLM reasoning, bridging the gap between transcriptomic data exploration and biological discovery. Code available at: https://github.com/omaruno/ELISA-An-AI-Agent-for-Expression-Grounded-Discovery-in-Single-Cell-Genomics.git (If you use ELISA in your research, please cite this work).",Omar Coser,2026.0,,2026-03-12,,"['arxiv', 'google_scholar', 'semantic_scholar']",3,[],3,,,,2026-03-01_to_2026-04-14,400,"{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""natural language concept, semantic matching, LLM-mediated interpretation"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""unifies scGPT expression embeddings with BioBERT-based semantic retrieval and LLM-mediated interpretation"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""wrapper_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""ELISA is a framework that integrates existing scGPT, BioBERT, and LLM for interactive single-cell analysis, not a new generative text-bio foundational model; thus it is an application wrapper.""}",application_wrapper,yes,yes,yes,application_wrapper,none,"natural language concept, semantic matching, LLM-mediated interpretation",unifies scGPT expression embeddings with BioBERT-based semantic retrieval and LLM-mediated interpretation,not_assessed,wrapper_boundary,"ELISA is a framework that integrates existing scGPT, BioBERT, and LLM for interactive single-cell analysis, not a new generative text-bio foundational model; thus it is an application wrapper.","{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""no"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_