ive biomarker discovery using an AI-driven, foundational-model-based framework.\n \n \n \n Katherina C. Chua, Yun-Ching Chen, Ariel Chen, Stewart Bates, Mehdi Pirooznia, Assieh Saadatpour. Integrative multi-omics characterization and AI-driven biomarker discovery for NSCLC stage III outcomes [abstract]. In: Proceedings of the American Association for Cancer Research Annual Meeting 2026; Part 1 (Regular Abstracts); 2026 Apr 17-22; San Diego, CA. Philadelphia (PA): AACR; Cancer Res 2026;86(7 Suppl):Abstract nr 1056.","doi":"10.1158/1538-7445.am2026-1056","year":"2026","venue":"Cancer Research","sources":["semantic_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003465","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a multimodal AI framework on tumor genomic/transcriptomic data and foundation-model representations, but no substantive text/language component is present. It is a primary model paper, but outside the text-bio scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrating heterogeneous genomic and transcriptomic data\" and \"COMPASS, a foundation model encoding RNA profiles\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_003465","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a biomarker-discovery framework that integrates COMPASS and another predictive model. No genuinely generative architecture is described.","evidence_snippet":"\"a multimodal AI framework combining contrastive learning and foundational-model representations\" and \"integration of two recently published models\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"EC2_no_text_component","adjudication_reason